// Original question bank for تحدّي العقول (Brain Battle).
//
// This is a *starting* bank, not an exhaustive one — over 300 hand-written questions
// across 6 challenge types, weighted toward hard/expert. It's deliberately hand-authored
// rather than imported from English trivia APIs (OpenTDB, The Trivia API, etc.) and
// machine-translated: four of the six challenge types here (proverbs, scramble,
// hidden-word, riddles) are language-native and don't have a meaningful English source to
// translate *from* — translating an English riddle doesn't produce an Arabic riddle, it
// produces nonsense. Only mcq_general could in principle be sourced that way, and
// community trivia databases are known to contain factual errors I'd have no way to
// verify at scale — so general-knowledge questions are hand-written from well-established
// facts too, same as everything else. This keeps the accuracy bar consistent across the
// whole bank at the cost of volume — reaching into the thousands would mean either
// accepting lower-confidence imported content or more authoring passes like this one.
// rather than padded with filler: every mcq_general item below sticks to extremely
// well-established, verifiable facts (capitals, standard historical dates, textbook
// science), every proverb is a widely-attested canonical one quoted as commonly known
// (not a rare/disputed variant), and every riddle is original/self-consistent rather than
// a claimed folk attribution I can't verify. Adding more later is just appending objects
// here — `battleLogic.ts` never needs to change.
//
// Deliberately excluded from v1: image-based questions (ماذا ترى؟) — needs real,
// licensed image assets this project doesn't have — and true semantic-embedding "secret
// word" proximity (Contexto's actual mechanic) — needs a word-embedding model/vector
// backend this stack has no infrastructure for. "الكلمة المخفية" below is the simpler,
// infra-free progressive-clue variant the brief also explicitly lists.

